WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.881 --> 00:00:19.688
The next morning we were unable to wash because the water in our pitchers had frozen overnight.

2
00:00:20.849 --> 00:00:26.511
The wind whistled through the cracks in our bedroom windows, and by breakfast I was ready to perish

3
00:00:26.571 --> 00:00:27.232
from the cold.

4
00:00:28.456 --> 00:00:34.358
In the schoolroom the lessons seemed long and difficult because I was not used to memorizing.

5
00:00:35.579 --> 00:00:39.981
So I was glad when one of the teachers gave me a strip of muslin to hem.

6
00:00:41.281 --> 00:00:48.344
Most of the girls were sewing, but one class still stood around Miss Scatcherd's chair reading English history

7
00:00:48.404 --> 00:00:54.487
aloud. When the chapter had been read through twice, Miss Scatcherd quizzed the students.

8
00:00:55.827 --> 00:01:01.507
Many of them could not even respond, but Helen Burns always knew the right answer.

9
00:01:02.688 --> 00:01:10.294
I expected Miss Scatcherd to praise Helen for paying attention, but instead she cried out, "You dirty, disagreeable

10
00:01:10.354 --> 00:01:13.937
girl! You didn't clean your nails this morning!"

11
00:01:15.759 --> 00:01:18.701
Helen said nothing, and I wondered at her silence.

12
00:01:19.922 --> 00:01:25.407
Why didn't she explain that she hadn't been able to clean her nails or wash her face because

13
00:01:25.447 --> 00:01:26.708
the water was frozen?

14
00:01:27.996 --> 00:01:33.097
But I couldn't think about this for very long because my teacher needed me to help her wind

15
00:01:33.157 --> 00:01:34.038
a skein of thread.

16
00:01:35.278 --> 00:01:40.359
When I returned to my seat, I saw that Helen was now carrying a rod made from a

17
00:01:40.479 --> 00:01:43.120
bundle of twigs tied together at one end.

18
00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:49.042
She handed this to Miss Scatcherd, who instantly whipped her a dozen times.

19
00:01:50.322 --> 00:01:56.484
Not a tear rose to Helen's eye, but my hands shook so much from anger that I could

20
00:01:56.524 --> 00:01:57.144
not sew.

21
00:01:58.472 --> 00:02:01.474
In the evenings we had an hour of play in the schoolroom.

22
00:02:02.694 --> 00:02:06.777
That night I found Helen, sitting alone and reading by the fire.

23
00:02:07.957 --> 00:02:13.080
We talked about her home in the north of England and then I said, "You must want to

24
00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:13.940
leave Lowood."

25
00:02:15.721 --> 00:02:17.142
She seemed quite surprised.

26
00:02:18.343 --> 00:02:19.083
"No, why?

27
00:02:19.103 --> 00:02:24.426
I was sent here to get an education, and it would be foolish to leave before I have

28
00:02:24.446 --> 00:02:24.926
done so."

29
00:02:24.946 --> 00:02:27.888
"But Miss Scatcherd is so cruel to you!"

30
00:02:29.032 --> 00:02:30.993
"Cruel? Not at all.

31
00:02:32.013 --> 00:02:34.414
She dislikes my faults," explained Helen.

32
00:02:34.434 --> 00:02:36.935
"I seldom put my things in order.

33
00:02:37.976 --> 00:02:38.656
I'm careless.

34
00:02:39.656 --> 00:02:43.178
I forget rules and I read when I should be learning my lessons."

35
00:02:43.198 --> 00:02:47.720
"And if I were you, I'd dislike her," I said firmly.

36
00:02:47.740 --> 00:02:49.741
"I would resist her.

37
00:02:50.861 --> 00:02:55.303
If she struck me with that rod, I'd snatch it from her and break it under her nose!"

38
00:02:55.323 --> 00:02:58.688
"If you did," said Helen, "Mr.

39
00:02:58.748 --> 00:03:03.670
Brocklehurst would expel you from school, and that would be a great grief to your relatives.

40
00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:10.351
It's better to endure a beating patiently than to commit a hasty action that disgraces your family."

41
00:03:11.432 --> 00:03:12.572
But I disagreed.

42
00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:19.294
"When we are struck without reason, we should strike back hard to teach that person never to do

43
00:03:19.334 --> 00:03:19.794
it again."

44
00:03:20.974 --> 00:03:26.156
Helen hoped I would change my mind and reminded me that the Bible says we should love our

45
00:03:26.236 --> 00:03:29.161
enemies. "Then I should love Mrs.

46
00:03:29.241 --> 00:03:30.842
Reed, which I cannot do."

47
00:03:32.043 --> 00:03:37.567
Helen asked me to explain, so I described in great detail my unhappy life with my aunt and

48
00:03:37.607 --> 00:03:41.770
cousins. "Wouldn't you be happier if you tried to forget Mrs.

49
00:03:41.830 --> 00:03:44.212
Reed's severity and the anger it ignited?"

50
00:03:44.612 --> 00:03:45.193
she asked.

51
00:03:46.373 --> 00:03:48.535
But I couldn't be as forgiving as Helen.

52
00:03:49.816 --> 00:03:54.739
One afternoon, when I had been at Lowood for about three weeks, I sat with a slate in

53
00:03:54.779 --> 00:03:57.762
my hand, puzzling over a long division problem.

54
00:03:59.543 --> 00:04:02.805
I looked up, and there at the front of the schoolroom stood Mr.

55
00:04:02.845 --> 00:04:05.848
Brocklehurst, as tall and forbidding as ever.

56
00:04:07.089 --> 00:04:09.230
All the girls and teachers rose to their feet.

57
00:04:10.491 --> 00:04:15.515
I had been dreading his appearance because I knew that he would brand me as a bad child.

58
00:04:16.696 --> 00:04:22.400
He began to speak quietly to Miss Temple, and I quickly realized he was not talking about me.

59
00:04:23.612 --> 00:04:29.195
"In settling accounts with the housekeeper," he said, "I find that a snack of bread and cheese has

60
00:04:29.215 --> 00:04:31.916
been served twice to the girls in the past two weeks.

61
00:04:33.177 --> 00:04:37.119
Who added this innovation and by what authority?"

62
00:04:37.139 --> 00:04:40.741
"I am responsible for that," said Miss Temple.

63
00:04:40.761 --> 00:04:46.204
"On those days breakfast was so ill prepared that the girls could not possibly eat it."

64
00:04:47.316 --> 00:04:53.458
"You are aware that my plan for bringing up these girls does not include introducing them to luxury?"

65
00:04:53.838 --> 00:04:54.298
said Mr.

66
00:04:54.318 --> 00:04:58.999
Brocklehurst. "They need to learn patience and self-denial.

67
00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:05.301
If their meals are spoiled again, you should address them on the sufferings of the early Christians and

68
00:05:05.321 --> 00:05:06.801
the torments of the martyrs.

69
00:05:07.882 --> 00:05:10.762
You should not provide extra food."

70
00:05:11.883 --> 00:05:16.104
Miss Temple stared straight ahead, looking as pale and hard as marble.

71
00:05:17.224 --> 00:05:22.947
Mr. Brocklehurst majestically surveyed the whole school while I shrank down to avoid his gaze.

72
00:05:24.147 --> 00:05:27.949
Suddenly he opened his eyes as if he'd seen something shocking.

73
00:05:27.969 --> 00:05:29.809
"Miss Temple!

74
00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:32.311
Who is that girl with red hair?

75
00:05:33.491 --> 00:05:35.192
Why is her hair in curls?"

76
00:05:36.392 --> 00:05:38.313
His hand shook as he pointed.

77
00:05:38.333 --> 00:05:44.956
"That is Julia Severn and her hair curls naturally," Miss Temple replied quietly.

78
00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:48.842
"She is not conforming to the principles of this school.

79
00:05:50.023 --> 00:05:51.424
Her hair must be cut off!"

80
00:05:52.585 --> 00:05:57.028
He pointed to the oldest students and cried, "Tell these girls to face the wall!"

81
00:05:58.769 --> 00:06:00.810
Miss Temple did so, and Mr.

82
00:06:00.850 --> 00:06:04.493
Brocklehurst walked behind them, examining the braids in their hair.

83
00:06:04.513 --> 00:06:07.235
"All this hair must be cut off!"

84
00:06:07.615 --> 00:06:08.115
he ordered.

85
00:06:08.136 --> 00:06:14.280
"Surely they could arrange their hair in a less offensive manner," protested Miss Temple.

86
00:06:15.452 --> 00:06:21.615
"My mission is to teach them to clothe themselves soberly, not with braided hair and costly apparel."

87
00:06:22.756 --> 00:06:27.158
Meanwhile I had been holding my slate in front of my face to avoid detection.

88
00:06:28.359 --> 00:06:31.881
Suddenly the slate slipped from my hand with a loud crash!

89
00:06:33.182 --> 00:06:37.644
Everyone looked at me as I picked up my broken slate and prepared for the worst.

90
00:06:37.664 --> 00:06:40.005
"The new girl!"

91
00:06:40.485 --> 00:06:41.006
said Mr.

92
00:06:41.046 --> 00:06:44.988
Brocklehurst. "I have something to say regarding her.

93
00:06:46.292 --> 00:06:48.513
Let the child who broke her slate come forward!"

94
00:06:50.394 --> 00:06:54.596
Miss Temple guided me toward him and gently whispered, "Don't be afraid, Jane.

95
00:06:55.736 --> 00:06:58.537
I saw it was an accident; you won't be punished."

96
00:06:58.557 --> 00:07:03.199
"In another minute she will despise me," I said to myself.

97
00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:07.261
Mr. Brocklehurst forced me to stand on a high stool.

98
00:07:07.281 --> 00:07:09.682
"Do you see this girl?"

99
00:07:10.042 --> 00:07:10.482
he said.

100
00:07:10.502 --> 00:07:16.497
"Girls, you must be on your guard against her, and teachers, you must watch her.

101
00:07:17.598 --> 00:07:19.058
For this girl is a liar!

102
00:07:20.299 --> 00:07:24.101
I learned this from the kind and generous lady who raised her as her own.

103
00:07:25.282 --> 00:07:27.563
And how did this girl repay the good lady?

104
00:07:28.684 --> 00:07:30.585
With lies and ingratitude!"

105
00:07:31.765 --> 00:07:33.546
Mr. Brocklehurst prepared to go.

106
00:07:33.566 --> 00:07:39.309
"Let her stand for half an hour on that stool, and let no one speak to her for

107
00:07:39.329 --> 00:07:40.270
the rest of the day!"

108
00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:46.101
With that, he departed and I was left to my humiliating punishment.
